ing size is going to be  monotonically increasing  and actually it's not so on the right  hand side you see  the size of the matching when we have no  limits on the number of interviews and  the x-axis is the average number of  applications  and it's actually uh not hard to prove  this theoretically basically we're  running the deferred acceptance  algorithm  and with more applications it's like  we're  appending the lists so  with these longer lists with this longer  preference list  we definitely come up with a larger size  matchings  okay let me conclude  our main technical contributions are one  computing  the expected size of the matching as a  result of the deferred acceptance  algorithm  as a function of the limit on the number  of applications and interviews  and two we find the optimal way of  distributing  distributing the applications  when given a fixed average number of  applications  uh our work suggests two policy  recommendations  first is that if there is a limited  ability in granting interviews  we need to limit the number of  applications and sometimes we need to  severely limit the number of  applications that the applicants can  send  in order to achieve a larger size  matching  and the second is that the optimal  matching size is achieved by a fair  system where  all the applicants apply to the same  number of positions  i would like to mention two open  problems the first one is  relaxing that the preferences come from  uniform distributions  maybe that's the main step to make the  model more realistic  so fortunately there have been some work  on correlated distributions  but the usual assumption  is that the preferences of the  applicants  or the preferences of the positions are  almost identical  so our work is kind of the other extreme  case where the preferences are  completely random but it would be nice  to have some results um  in the between and the second open  problem  is to study other matching mechanisms  other than  the deferred acceptance algorithm um so  we still have the same  first stage but we're changing the  matching mechanism and to compare these  different mechanisms  that's all thank you so much for  watching


